There are five other entrances to the catacombs - three scattered around the surface of [[Great Kourend]] and two further entrances connecting to other dungeons on Great Kourend ([[Forthos Dungeon]] and [[Giants' Den]], respectively). However, these additional entrances will only appear once the player has climbed the respective [[Vine (Catacombs of Kourend)|vines]] from inside the Catacombs. The vines connecting to the surface are located in the dungeon map to the right, marked with a [[File:Map link icon.png]] icon.

==History==
The Catacombs of Kourend were created by [[Skotizo]] during the [[God Wars]] by using an artefact stolen from the [[Karamjan Temple]].{{CiteText|text=Mount Karuulm diary|author=Karuulm|quote=The arrival seems to be a demon of Zamorak, one in possession of an artefact I have never encountered. While the demon arrived alone, he has used this artefact to call upon a variety of creatures to his side.}} The Catacombs are said to belong in another realm,{{CiteNPC|npc=Kharedst's memoirs|quote=The entrance below may be below the earth, but that realm lies beyond the reach of us mere mortals.}} while also being beneath the kingdom.{{CiteNPC|npc=Konar quo Maten|quote=The Catacombs of Kourend are located beneath Great Kourend.}} The Catacombs are also enchanted with powerful magic that prevents the monsters within from escaping;{{CiteText|text=Kharedst's memoirs|author=Rose|quote=I know of the powerful magic that keeps them bound below.}} conversely, it is supposedly difficult for "mere mortals" to enter the Catacombs as well, though players can enter the area without issues.

==Transportation==
The fastest way to the main entrance is through [[Xeric's talisman]] with the "Xeric's Heart" function, which teleports the player outside the statue of [[King Rada I]], the [[Kourend Castle Teleport]] spell, which requires completion of [[Client of Kourend]], or using a [[Ring of returning]] having set your respawn point to Kourend Castle, which can only be done after completion of [[A Kingdom Divided]]. 

Alternate forms of transport include:

* [[Achievement diary cape]] to the Kourend & Kebos option, which puts the player next to [[Elise]].
* A portal in the [[portal chamber]] or [[portal nexus]] of a [[player-owned house]] attuned to Kourend Castle.
* Using the Hosidius page(Lunch by the Lancalliums) in the [[Kharedst's memoirs]]; or using the Hosidius page in the [[Book of the Dead]], after completion of [[A Kingdom Divided]]
* Fairy ring: {{Fairycode|djr}}.
* Fairy ring: {{Fairycode|cis}}.
* [[Games necklace]] to [[Wintertodt]], then [[Lovakengj Minecart Network]] to Kingstown
* [[Rada's blessing]] to [[Kourend Woodland]], then [[Lovakengj Minecart Network]] to Kingstown

==Features==
The Catacombs contain many [[Slayer monsters|monsters]] that are commonly assigned to players for [[Slayer tasks]], and are slightly stronger compared to those found elsewhere on [[Gielinor]]. As this particular dungeon is a [[multicombat area]] (excluding the [[brutal dragon]] area), it is generally recommended to use [[Prayer]] or high-healing methods for [[aggressive]] high-level monsters stacked against the player. In addition, '''[[dwarf multicannon]]s cannot be placed inside the Catacombs'''. If players attempt to place one, the chatbox will state "''The influence of the dark altar prevents your cannon being set up here.''"

A special effect of the Catacombs is that players who bury [[bones]] of any type within it will have a small amount of their [[Prayer points]] restored. This also applies if the bones are crushed via the [[bonecrusher]], although the Prayer restoration effect of the [[bonecrusher necklace]] does not stack. ''Note scattering [[Remains#Demonic ashes|demonic ashes]] does not restore Prayer points - only bones.''
*[[Bones]] restore 1 Prayer point.
*[[Big bones]] restore 2 Prayer points.
*[[Dragon bones]] restore 4 Prayer points.

There are also a few [[Agility shortcut]]s around the dungeon, the highest of them requiring 34 [[Agility]]. These shortcuts are found in the following areas:

*[[Crack (Southern Catacombs of Kourend)|Southern Crevice]]: Two-way shortcut between [[cyclops]] and [[ankou]]. Requires 17 Agility.
*[[Stones (Catacombs of Kourend)|Stepping stones]]: Two-way shortcut between the [[steel dragon]] and [[brutal red dragon]] area. Requires 28 Agility. Each stepping stone must be clicked on to jump to it. Steel/brutal red dragons can attack players while using the shortcut.
*[[Crack (Northern Catacombs of Kourend)|Northern Crevice]]: Two-way shortcut between [[warped jellies]] and [[greater nechryael]]. Requires 34 Agility.
There is a non-agility shortcut:
*[[Rocks (Catacombs of Kourend)|Rocks]] shortcut between skeletons and possessed pickaxes. Requires [[pickaxe]] to mine and will regenerate after being passed through.

The [[Altar (Catacombs of Kourend)|dark altar]] in the main entrance of the catacombs can be used to teleport to the four sections of the Catacombs; doing so requires using an [[ancient shard]], which is obtained from monsters in the catacombs.

===Demon's Run===
[[File:Catacombs of Kourend - Demon's Run.png|thumb|right|The Demon's Run]]
The Demon's Run is the north-eastern section of the Catacombs, where various demonic creatures can be found. An unattackable [[Man (Catacombs of Kourend)|man]] can also be found wandering here. The exit is found in the north-east corner with the [[greater demon]]s, which leads up to the hole west of the [[dense essence mine]].

Once the exit has been used it can be quickly accessed via [[fairy ring]] {{Fairycode|cis}} and running east.

